        "prompt": "You are searching the Kubernetes source repo (repo id: github.com/sg-evals/kubernetes--v1.32.0) via the mcp__retrieval__* tools (list_files, read_file, definition, references, submit_files). This is a read-only research task \u2014 do not modify anything, just report file paths and short quoted evidence.\n\nContext: I'm investigating a support ticket about kube-apiserver failing readyz during a rolling upgrade from v1.32 to v1.33, with these log lines:\n\n1. `PostStartHook \"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\" failed: unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check` \u2014 I already found this is generated in pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go (the PostStartHook function using async.Runner and a 1-minute timeout).\n\n2. `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"10.211.95.185\" is forbidden: not yet ready to handle request` \u2014 I need you to find EXACTLY where this error string (or the equivalent \"not ready to handle request\" / \"not yet ready\" message) is generated. My strong hypothesis is it's in the IP allocator code under pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/ \u2014 likely a \"meta allocator\" (cidrallocator.go or similar) that wraps the bitmap allocator and the new IPAddress-API-backed allocator, and blocks/rejects allocation until its informers have synced. Look at files like:\n   - pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/cidrallocator.go\n   - pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/ipallocator.go\n   - pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/interfaces.go\n   Read whichever of these exist and quote the exact code that produces a \"forbidden ... not yet ready\" style error (likely a k8s.io/apimachinery apierrors.NewForbidden or similar call gated on an informer HasSynced check or a sync.Once/atomic readiness flag).\n\n3. The readyz endpoint check name `informer-sync,poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` \u2014 I need you to find where the generic apiserver registers an \"informer-sync\" readyz health check. This is likely in one of:\n   - staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/config.go\n   - staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz/healthz.go\n   - staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/genericapiserver.go\n   - or a dedicated file registering `healthz.NamedCheck(\"informer-sync\", ...)` tied to SharedInformerFactory.WaitForCacheSync\n   Find the exact registration site and quote it.\n\nFor each of the 3 items above, report: the exact file path (repo-relative), the relevant function/type name, and a short quoted code snippet as evidence. Also note any other file that's clearly part of the causal chain (e.g. the MetaAllocator struct definition, the ControllerName constant, or where the \"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\" hook is wired to readyz via WithHealthChecks/AddPostStartHook semantics \u2014 post-start hooks automatically become readyz checks named \"poststarthook/<name>\" in generic apiserver, find that mechanism too if you can, likely in staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz or genericapiserver.go's AddPostStartHookOrDie / healthz check wiring).\n\nFinish by calling submit_files (or just report \u2014 you don't have submit_files, so just report in your final message) with the list of every file you found relevant, most important first, and a concise summary (under 400 words) with the file:line-ish evidence quotes.",
