  "cli_result_text": "I've traced the full causal chain for this ticket and submitted the relevant files. Summary of what each piece contributes:\n\n**1. Where the error is generated**\n- `pkg/registry/core/rest/storage_core.go` \u2014 the `legacyProvider.PostStartHook()` function registers the hook literally named `\"start-service-ip-repair-controllers\"`, spins up both the ClusterIP and NodePort repair loops via `async.Runner`, waits on a `sync.WaitGroup`, and if neither reports success within **1 minute**, returns `goerrors.New(\"unable to perform initial IP and Port allocation check\")` \u2014 the exact string from the ticket.\n\n**2. The repair/allocation chain that has to succeed within that 1-minute window**\n- `pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/controller/repairip.go` (`RepairIPAddress.RunUntil`) \u2014 before doing anything else, it polls for the **default ServiceCIDR object** to exist (`defaultservicecidr.DefaultServiceCIDRName`), then runs `runOnce()` reconciling every Service's ClusterIP against `IPAddress` objects, calling `IPAddresses().Create()` directly for any missing ones (this is what produces the `ipaddresses.networking.k8s.io \"10.211.95.185\" is forbidden` error during the create).\n- `pkg/registry/core/service/ipallocator/cidrallocator.go` (`MetaAllocator`) and `ipallocator.go` (`Allocator`) \u2014 allocation only proceeds once `allocator.ready` is `true`, which is driven entirely by the `ServiceCIDR` object's `Ready` status **condition** (`isReady()`), not just informer sync.\n\n**3. Readyz propagation mechanism**\n- `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/hooks.go` \u2014 every `AddPostStartHook` call auto-registers a `postStartHookHealthz` check named `\"poststarthook/<name>\"` on livez/readyz. Critically, `runPostStartHook` calls `klog.Fatalf` if the hook returns an error \u2014 so the 1-minute timeout doesn't just fail readyz, it **kills the apiserver process**.\n- `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/healthz.go` (`AddBootSequenceHealthChecks`) and `pkg/controlplane/apiserver/aggregator.go` register the sibling `\"informer-sync\"` boot-sequence check that appears alongside it in the readyz output.\n- `staging/src/k8s.io/apiserver/pkg/server/genericapiserver.go` / `storage_readiness_hook.go` / `registry/rest/rest.go` / `generic/registry/store.go` \u2014 the general `StorageWithReadiness`/`ReadinessCheck` machinery gating REST storage until backing etcd/informer state is ready.\n\n**The race**: during a mixed v1.32/v1.33 rolling upgrade, the default `ServiceCIDR`'s `Ready` condition (and/or its informer sync) can lag or flap depending on which apiserver version last wrote/observed it, so `MetaAllocator`/`Allocator.ready` stays false past the hard-coded 1-minute deadline in `storage_core.go`, the PostStartHook returns an error, `klog.Fatalf` kills the process, and readyz reports both `informer-sync` and `poststarthook/start-service-ip-repair-controllers` as failed \u2014 explaining why it self-heals once every node is on the same version.",
